Executor
├── initialization and caller
│   ├── binds one immutable adapter at deployment
│   ├── defaults to no authorized caller
│   ├── only the owner can select the caller or replace configured actions
│   ├── rotating or clearing the caller immediately removes old execution permission
│   ├── the owner has no implicit execution permission
│   └── the selected caller needs no adapter leaf roles
├── configured actions
│   ├── store only liquidity target, query calldata, and leaf for each action
│   ├── funding entries precede zero-target final-batch entries
│   ├── replacements remove obsolete sources even when their Merkle roles remain
│   ├── empty configuration disables execution even with idle funds
│   ├── repeated executions preserve configuration while using different wildcard amounts
│   └── callbacks cannot replace actions or change the caller during execution
├── caller-supplied Merkle actions
│   ├── require one call per configured entry in the same order
│   ├── reject changed target, value, mask, or pinned calldata
│   ├── reject missing, inserted, reordered, or duplicated entries
│   ├── final-operation leaves must match configuration too
│   └── execute encoded amounts without rewriting calldata
├── liquidity preparation
│   ├── spend idle funds above the protected reserve first
│   ├── query each needed source immediately before use
│   ├── require full source capacity before advancing unless remaining need is smaller
│   ├── reject underuse, overuse, or balance decreases and roll back every effect
│   ├── skip zero-capacity and unnecessary sources without shifting final-batch indices
│   └── preserve static query semantics and bubble query failures
├── adapter authorization
│   ├── executed leaves require current proofs and Executor roles
│   ├── caller leaf roles do not bypass the configured caller restriction
│   ├── skipped funding calls need no Executor role
│   └── invalid final proofs roll back earlier funding
├── final operation
│   ├── Liquid Lane targets the bound adapter's connector
│   ├── ThreeF targets the bound adapter and reads its live maker authorization
│   ├── reject unsupported operations, invalid bounds, or changed funding requirements
│   └── require the final batch to spend exactly its operation amount
└── atomicity
    ├── retain pending allocation and matured deallocation reserves
    ├── revert prior withdrawals when a borrow health floor or asset budget fails
    └── reject reentry without retaining transfers, approvals, usage, or debt
